description:
I am getting an error `Error in pieces[[2]] : subscript out of bounds` when running devtools::load_all()

Below is my output of traceback()

```
5: (function (dep_name, dep_ver = "*") 
   {
       if (dep_name == "R") {
           return(TRUE)
       }
       if (!requireNamespace(dep_name, quietly = TRUE)) {
           warning("Dependency package '", dep_name, "' not available.")
           return(FALSE)
       }
       if (dep_ver == "*") {
           return(TRUE)
       }
       pieces <- strsplit(dep_ver, "[[:space:]]+")[[1]]
       dep_compare <- pieces[[1]]
       dep_ver <- pieces[[2]]
       compare <- match.fun(dep_compare)
       if (!compare(as.numeric_version(getNamespaceVersion(dep_name)), 
           as.numeric_version(dep_ver))) {
           warning("Need ", dep_name, " ", dep_compare, " ", dep_ver, 
               " but loaded version is ", getNamespaceVersion(dep_name), 
               call. = FALSE)
       }
       return(TRUE)
   })(dots[[1L]][[1L]], dots[[2L]][[1L]])
4: mapply(check_dep_version, depends$package, depends$version)
3: load_depends(path)
2: pkgload::load_all(path = path, reset = reset, recompile = recompile, 
       export_all = export_all, helpers = helpers, quiet = quiet, 
       ...)
1: devtools::load_all("~/git_repos/phd/thesis/")
```

From what I understand, pieces[[2]] should contain a dependency version. So I tried putting a required version for  all my packages in DESCRIPTION. This did not help.

Would appreciate any help!

I am on macOS 11.4, running R 4.1.0

Thanks!
